Let me look at how the PDU options are parsed and how coap_opt_value/coap_opt_length work, to understand the buffer boundaries. The key is that coap_split_proxy_uri is called with coap_opt_value(q) and coap_opt_length(q). The option value is a pointer into the PDU buffer. If the option length is wrong or the value extends beyond the buffer, then coap_split_uri_sub reading beyond could overflow.
